{{Navbar-Global Gas Infrastructure Tracker}}
'''Targa Resources Pipeline System''' is a proposed natural gas pipeline in the United States.<ref name="rca4bf9">{{Cite web|url=https://pgjonline.com/news/2026/august/targa-plans-70-mi-permian-gas-pipeline-to-expand-waha-takeaway-capacity|title=pgjonline.com|website=pgjonline.com|access-date=2026-11-04}}</ref><ref name="r2ebb68">{{Cite web|url=https://www.ogj.com/refining-processing/news/55398842/targa-adding-midstream-infrastructure-amid-new-permian-agreements-with-exxonmobil|title=ogj.com|website=ogj.com|access-date=2026-11-04}}</ref><ref name="r030377">{{Cite web|url=https://www.manilatimes.net/2026/08/18/tmt-newswire/globenewswire/targa-resources-corp-announces-20-year-agreements-with-exxonmobil-and-announces-three-new-natural-gas-processing-plants-in-the-permian-delaware/2407144|title=manilatimes.net|website=manilatimes.net|access-date=2026-11-04}}</ref>

==Location==
The pipeline is proposed to run from Texas to Waha Hub, Texas.<ref name="rca4bf9" /><ref name="r2ebb68" /><ref name="r030377" />

==Project Details==
*'''Owner: '''Targa Resources Corp<ref name="rca4bf9" /><ref name="r030377" />
*'''Length: '''70 mi<ref name="rca4bf9" /><ref name="r2ebb68" /><ref name="r030377" />
*'''Status: '''Proposed<ref name="rca4bf9" /><ref name="r2ebb68" /><ref name="r030377" />

==Background==
Targa announced Bull Run II on August 18, 2026, together with new 20-year agreements with ExxonMobil. The line would be added to Targa's existing Bull Run residue gas system. It would carry gas from three planned Delaware basin processing plants, Wrangler, Ranger and Ranger II.<ref name="r2ebb68" /><ref name="rca4bf9" />

The plants would total about 825 million cubic feet per day. Take-or-pay commitments would back the pipeline. Targa said it expected operations to begin in the first half of 2028.<ref name="r2ebb68" /><ref name="rca4bf9" />

